<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13319" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπονόσφι</span></b> , before a vowel <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπονοστ-νόσφιν</span></b> , 
			Ep.
		
		Adv.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>far apart, aloof,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. κατίσχεαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					2.233
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τραπέσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					5.350
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> c. gen.,
			following its case, <i>far away from,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμεῦ ἀ. ἐόντα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					1.541
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φίλων ἀ. ὀλέσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					5.113
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φίλων ἀ. ἑταίρων</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				12.33
			</span></i>.</div>
